      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done, see the updated comment above the declaration.\n\nFor `/data/user/[0-9]` and `/data/data`, the security contexts of their subdirectories are based on seapp_contexts (instead of file_contexts). Right now, because they are caught by is_app_data_path(), they are also implicitly skipped. This is working because we don\u0027t use SELINUX_ANDROID_RESTORECON_DATADATA with SELINUX_ANDROID_RESTORECON_SKIPCE. But there is nothing in the code to prevent that from happening. I can follow up with a separate change to make sure these flags are XOR. Thanks.",
